ull,"comments":3,"created_at":"2022-07-05T15:25:05Z","updated_at":"2022-07-12T13:18:07Z","closed_at":"2022-07-12T13:18:07Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Describe the bug**\r\n\r\nWhen a user is banished (for spam) their podcast submissions are not removed, and clog up the queue in `/admin/content_manager/podcasts`.\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\n\r\n1. Create a burner account on Forem\r\n2. Submit a podcast via `/podcasts/new`\r\n3. Log into another account with admin credentials\r\n4. Banish the burner account\r\n5. Navigate to `/admin/content_manager/podcasts`\r\n6. See that podcast is still there\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\n\r\nWhen a user is banished, their podcast submissions should be deleted in the process.\r\n\r\n**Screenshots**\r\n\r\n![Screen Shot 2022-07-05 at 11 20 47 AM](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/16007075/177362620-ea2a4975-c0c4-4807-a6cb-4afc07e069a7.png)\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\n\r\nThis may be considered a feature request, but I think the lack of this feature is buggy — we always delete all content from banished users, so I think this is just an area that we missed.\r\n\r\nAlso, here is a related feature request that should also be tackled - https://github.com/forem/forem/discussions/16702 ... currently there is no way for an admin managing podcast to delete any submissions. As such, spammy/junk submissions cannot be removed.","closed_by":{"login":"jeremyf","id":2130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyf","html_url":"https://github.com/jeremyf","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jeremyf/following{/other_user}","gists_url